{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2184-05-08 05:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I'm Dr. Lee, one of the hospitalists. You're here today because of abdominal pain and some dizziness when standing up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2184-05-08 05:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that's right. The pain is my usual, but the dizziness is new. I felt really lightheaded yesterday after standing up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2184-05-08 05:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. In the ER, your vitals showed a fast heart rate—133—and your blood pressure was 147 over 87. You got IV fluids and some Dilaudid for pain, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2184-05-08 05:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, 2 mg total. It helped the pain, but I still felt shaky and like I might pass out when I stood up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2184-05-08 05:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked your orthostatic vitals. Your blood pressure didn’t drop much, but your heart rate went up from 103 lying down to 120 standing. That’s what we call subjective orthostasis—your symptoms don’t fully match the numbers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2184-05-08 05:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not really low blood pressure? But it feels so real."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2184-05-08 05:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It is real to you, and we take that seriously. Dehydration can contribute, and you mentioned you didn’t drink much yesterday and had over eight bowel movements."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2184-05-08 05:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve been having looser stools. But no vomiting or fever."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2184-05-08 05:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs show mild dehydration—BUN is 24, which supports that. But your blood count, kidney function, and urine are otherwise normal. No infection signs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2184-05-08 05:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Could my meds be causing this? I’ve been anxious lately with the holiday coming up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2184-05-08 05:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a good point. Both clonidine and Abilify can cause dizziness and a fast heart rate. You recently increased the dose of both, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2184-05-08 05:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, Abilify was increased a few months ago. I’ve been on 2 mg, but now it’s higher."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2184-05-08 05:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We spoke with your primary care doctor. Since your symptoms started around the time of the dose increase, we recommend lowering Abilify back to 2 mg daily—the dose you were on before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2184-05-08 05:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. I tried calling my psych doctor, but they weren’t available."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2184-05-08 05:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We documented the change and recommend you follow up with them soon. Your abdominal pain is at your usual baseline, so we didn’t change your pain plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2184-05-08 05:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad. I just needed the IV pain meds like I get in the ER every few weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2184-05-08 05:41:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We also did a chest X-ray to check for pneumonia since your heart rate is high, but it’s clear. No lung or heart issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2184-05-08 05:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good to know. So I can go home today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2184-05-08 05:43:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’re stable. We’ll send you home with instructions to reduce Abilify and follow up with your doctors. Keep monitoring how you feel when standing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2184-05-08 05:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my TPN? I need to restart that at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2184-05-08 05:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, continue your home TPN as usual. All your other meds stay the same except Abilify."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2184-05-08 05:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’ll call my psych doctor this week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2184-05-08 05:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. We’ll also note that your Free T4 was slightly low—your primary may want to check your thyroid dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2184-05-08 05:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had hypothyroidism for years. My dose is usually stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2184-05-08 05:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just something to keep an eye on. Otherwise, you’re cleared to go home. A nurse will give you discharge papers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2184-05-08 05:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate all your help. The dizziness was really worrying me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2184-05-08 05:51:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. It’s good we found a likely cause. Take care, and don’t hesitate to reach out if symptoms change."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2184-05-08 05:52:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee. I’ll follow up as recommended."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2184-05-08 05:25:00",
    "admission_end": "2184-05-08 16:27:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a complex history of sclerosing mesenteritis, recurrent small bowel obstruction, and 23 prior abdominal surgeries was admitted for management of chronic abdominal pain and new-onset subjective orthostatic dizziness. She received her established ED pain protocol with IV Dilaudid and IV fluids for dehydration. Evaluation revealed no acute infection or cardiopulmonary process. Her dizziness was not fully explained by orthostatic vital signs but was likely related to recent dose increases in clonidine and Abilify. The decision was made to reduce Abilify to her prior dose of 2 mg daily, with close follow-up recommended. Her abdominal pain remained at baseline, and she continued home TPN. She was discharged home in stable condition with instructions to monitor symptoms and follow up with her primary care and psychiatric providers.",
